preConditionHook:
// THE CORPUS'S SWING-PIVOT PRIMITIVE. Fires on the bar a swing high is
// CONFIRMED: the bar `strength` bars ago is a pivot, which is knowable only
// now, `strength` bars after it printed. That lag is what makes the rule
// lookahead-safe. Detection only -- retaining the pivot's price for a later
// comparison is separate machinery (BreakoutLevelRetest inlines its own copy
// of this scan rather than depending on this file).
//
// This mirrors EasyLanguage's SwingHighBar(1, high, strength, lookback) and
// SwingLowBar, which the twin calls. There is no WFSafe_SwingHigh in the
// MultiWalk library -- Brian checked the function list -- so plain EL governs
// here, unlike every other series function in the corpus.
//
// MEASURED, EL_Swing_Probe.txt / el_swing_output1.txt (@ES 60 min, 100 bars,
// pattern period-8 stable on 76/76 bars from bar 25):
//
//   * THE PIVOT TEST IS MIXED, not at-or-above on both sides. The pivot bar
//     is AT OR ABOVE the `strength` OLDER bars and STRICTLY ABOVE the
//     `strength` NEWER bars, so a flat top yields exactly ONE pivot -- the
//     LATER of the equal bars -- and never N of them (the probe's flat top
//     reported bar 4, never bar 3, on 95/95 bars). This REFUTES the merged
//     pseudocode, which took Brooks's symmetric glossary wording and used
//     >= on both sides. Where a rule's source is Brooks's prose and its
//     implementation is SwingHigh, the two differ on flat bars, and the
//     corpus follows EasyLanguage.
//   * CONFIRMATION LAG is exactly `strength` bars: the smallest bars-ago
//     ever returned was 2 at strength 2, never 0 or 1. No lookahead.
//   * THE -1 SENTINEL is real -- on a strictly rising ramp with no pivot the
//     function returned -1 on 100/100 bars, and it does not degrade to "the
//     highest bar seen". It is guarded explicitly below even though -1 can
//     never equal a positive `strength`, because -1 as a PRICE sits under
//     every real price and the habit has to be universal.
//   * `lookback` is EL's Length: candidate offsets 0..lookback-1 counted
//     from the current bar INCLUSIVE. A pivot older than that returns -1
//     rather than falling back to an earlier one, so the reportable range is
//     strength..lookback-1 and lookback <= strength can never fire.
//     lookback does NOT have to exceed 2*strength+1: the neighbourhood test
//     reaches `strength` bars PAST the window (a bars-ago-4 pivot was
//     reported under Length 5), which is why the deepest index touched is
//     lookback - 1 + strength.
//   * THE COMPARISONS CARRY THE 2.22e-12 RELATIONAL TOLERANCE. EL's standard
//     functions are themselves EasyLanguage, so the scan uses el_gt / el_ge
//     and not raw > and >=: on the probe's tolerance series the two disagree
//     about WHICH bar is the pivot, not merely at the last bit.
//
// The low side's TIE sense is the mirror of the measured high-side rule
// rather than an observation -- the probe's flat-extreme series was a flat
// TOP only. A flat-bottom series would settle it.
//
// Scanning newest-first with a break reproduces "occurrence 1 is the most
// recent confirmed pivot". Unmeasured and unused here: lookback below
// strength+1, lookback = 0, and occurrence 3 or more.
const int pivStrength = (int)strength;
const int pivWindow = (int)lookback;
pivotHighBar = -1;
for (int j = pivStrength; j <= pivWindow - 1; ++j) {
    bool ok = true;
    for (int k = j - pivStrength; k < j; ++k) {
        if (!el_gt(high[j], high[k])) { ok = false; break; }
    }
    if (ok) {
        for (int k = j + 1; k <= j + pivStrength; ++k) {
            if (!el_ge(high[j], high[k])) { ok = false; break; }
        }
    }
    if (ok) { pivotHighBar = j; break; }
}
pivotLowBar = -1;
for (int j = pivStrength; j <= pivWindow - 1; ++j) {
    bool ok = true;
    for (int k = j - pivStrength; k < j; ++k) {
        if (!el_lt(low[j], low[k])) { ok = false; break; }
    }
    if (ok) {
        for (int k = j + 1; k <= j + pivStrength; ++k) {
            if (!el_le(low[j], low[k])) { ok = false; break; }
        }
    }
    if (ok) { pivotLowBar = j; break; }
}
swingHighNow = (pivotHighBar != -1) && (pivotHighBar == pivStrength);
swingLowNow = (pivotLowBar != -1) && (pivotLowBar == pivStrength);
